# Espruino — system overview
# A thin fork-origin note: an untouched mirror of espruino/Espruino.
# Zones run left to right: origin -> core -> state -> external.
# Style classes set strokes only, so light and dark stay readable.

title: |md
  # Espruino
  A JavaScript interpreter for microcontrollers, small enough for 128 kB flash and 8 kB RAM.
| {near: top-center}

direction: right
grid-columns: 2
grid-rows: 2
horizontal-gap: 170
vertical-gap: 110

origin: Origin {
  direction: down

  upstream: `espruino/Espruino` · Gordon Williams · MPL 2.0
  mirror: `d3nd3/Espruino` · one docs commit of ours · still 71 behind upstream
  dirt: untracked `compile_commands.json` · a local build artefact, not ours to commit
  reading: `README_BuildProcess.md` is the real architecture text, the README is a shop front
  protocol: `README_Protocol.md` documents the wire format the IDE speaks
}

state: State {
  direction: down

  flash: `save()` pretokenises code and stores it in flash, re-read on every boot
  ram: one flat JsVar array · its size is `variables` in the board file, and overflow shows up at build time
  build: `gen/`, `build/`, `obj/` · gitignored and regenerated per board
}

core: Core {
  direction: down

  board: `boards/BOARD.py` · 60 board files — pins, RAM, console, variable count
  gen: `scripts/build_platform_config.py`, `build_pininfo.py`, `build_jswrapper.py`, `build_linker.py` → `gen/`
  interp: `src/jsparse.c` · recursive-descent parser that executes as it walks, behind `src/jslex.c`
  heap: `src/jsvar.c` · every JS value is a reference-counted JsVar slot, not a real object
  natives: `src/jswrap_*.c` · 96 wrapper files, `gen/jswrapper.c` is the flash symbol table lookup
  ports: `targets/nrf5x`, `stm32`, `stm32_ll`, `esp32`, `esp8266`, `linux`, `emscripten`
  jslibs: `libs/` · feature C libs plus `libs/js/*.min.js` modules listed per board and embedded in flash
}

ext: External {
  direction: down

  tooling: EspruinoTools and the Web IDE · serial, BLE or TCP on port 23, `>` prompt protocol
  sdk: nRF5 SDK, STM32 HAL, ESP-IDF · per target, referenced rather than committed
  toolchain: arm-none-eabi-gcc, xtensa · gitignored, supplied by whoever builds
  site: espruino.com · docs, nightly binaries, board JSON
}

origin -> core: upstream tree, unmodified
core -> state: tokenised code in flash, JsVar heap in RAM
core -> ext: built against an SDK, driven by the IDE

classes: {
  origin: {style: {stroke: "#2f6fbf"}}
  core: {style: {stroke: "#2f8f5f"}}
  state: {style: {stroke: "#a86a12"; stroke-dash: 3}}
  ext: {style: {stroke: "#8a4fbf"; stroke-dash: 5}}
}

origin.class: origin
core.class: core
state.class: state
ext.class: ext
